STEP 4 — the first declarations, measured. A one-shot script in the session scratchpad (never committed) runs AFTER step 2 is in the tree: it computes, from inspector.encapsulation_breaches(repo_root) before any field exists, per target component T, sorted(set(module of every breach with reason 'undeclared')) — only the legal-kind edges; 'into_device' breaches are excluded by construction and stay red. Devices and every other component with no such importer get []. For each of the 83 charters: read the text; if it already carries "public_interface", leave it and print it; else insert the field textually, never re-serializing: replace the text's final "
}" with ",
  "public_interface": <json.dumps(list)>
}" and write it through cairn.tools.artifact.artifact.write(path, text, verb="charter", why="56d1aff4455e: first public_interface declaration, measured (RULE 1)"). Then openai_wire's charter: its falsifier clause (a) text "the machine_imports_no_device sieve says so" becomes "the encapsulation_holds sieve says so" through the same door, same verb. Re-run encapsulation_breaches: zero 'undeclared' and zero 'missing_field' remain.
